# /research/ was renamed to /projects/ (2026-07-30). These rules keep every
# old URL alive, which matters for more than bookmarks: App Store builds
# already in the wild fetch /research/projects/<folder>/index.md. URLSession
# follows 301s, so those installs keep working until the next release ships.
#
# The technology.json and technology/ rules were dropped 2026-07-30 with the toy catalog itself.
# The shipped App Store build's Research tab fetches that file and will show an
# error until a new build ships — the replacement gallery tab needs no such
# file.
#
# Project folders also lost a path segment in the move
# (/research/projects/X/ → /projects/X/), so that prefix needs its own rule
# that collapses the extra segment.
#
# ⚠️ Every source pattern here is DISJOINT on purpose. A catch-all
# `/research/* → /projects/:splat` alongside the more specific
# `/research/projects/*` rule looked correct and was not: Workers Static
# Assets did not honour first-match-wins by file order, the catch-all won,
# and /research/projects/X/ resolved to /projects/projects/X/ (404). Do not
# reintroduce an overlapping catch-all — enumerate instead.
#
# THE SECOND RENAME (2026-08-01): gallery → thewall. The wall's manifest and
# its picture folder were renamed to match the name the thing has always had in
# prose. Shipped App Store builds hardcode /projects/gallery.json in
# APIClient.swift, so that URL has to keep answering — and because the manifest
# it now redirects to points its tiles at /projects/thewall/..., the picture
# folder needs its own rule for anything holding an older copy of the JSON.
# The /research/gallery.json rule below points straight at the new name rather
# than chaining through the old one — one hop, not two.
#
# THE THIRD RENAME (2026-08-01): curriculum/source → curriculum/content. The
# folder holds the per-discipline markdown tables, and "source" read as though it
# were build input when it is in fact the published artifact (the .docx sources
# were dropped in f8e7ad3 — this IS the content now).
#
# ⚠️ Shipped App Store builds hardcode https://vivianweidai.com/curriculum/source/
# in CurriculumLoader.swift, so that prefix has to keep answering or the
# Curriculum tab breaks in every installed copy until a new release ships. The
# website's own web/src/layouts/curriculum.js was updated in place and does not
# rely on this rule.

# THE FOURTH RENAME (2026-08-01): a project's index.md → report.md. "index" only
# ever described the file's position in a folder; the thing is a report.
#
# ⚠️ TheWallTile.swift builds this URL AT RUNTIME (href + "/index.md") in every
# shipped build, so tapping a project card in an installed copy fetches the old
# name. This rule is what keeps the in-app markdown reader working until the next
# release. Builds older than 1.5.6 use /research/projects/<folder>/index.md and
# are NOT covered — chaining through the /research/ rule would need two hops, and
# an overlapping specific rule loses to the catch-all (see the warning above).
# Those builds already have a broken tech browser; this is not a new regression.

# THE FIFTH RENAME (2026-08-01): the wall's manifest moved INTO its own folder,
# /projects/thewall.json → /projects/thewall/thewall.json, so the yml, the json
# and the pictures all sit together the way every other area is arranged.
#
# ⚠️ APIClient.swift hardcodes the old URL in every shipped build, so that path
# must keep answering. The two gallery.json rules above were re-pointed at the
# NEW location rather than chaining through the old one — one hop, not two.

# Served by Cloudflare Workers Static Assets, which reads this file from the
# assets directory. The Worker itself is still a pure passthrough.

/research/projects/*     /projects/:splat             301
/research/gallery.json   /projects/thewall/thewall.json   301
/research/               /projects/                   301
/research                 /projects                   301

/projects/gallery.json   /projects/thewall/thewall.json   301
/projects/gallery/*      /projects/thewall/:splat     301

/curriculum/source/*     /curriculum/content/:splat    301
/projects/:folder/index.md   /projects/:folder/report.md   301
/projects/thewall.json   /projects/thewall/thewall.json   301
